%erg 0.1
Title: ticket-only PRs carry a self-closing Ticket close claim on the ticket they create
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: haduong

--- log ---
2026-11-09T19:17Z haduong created

--- body ---
## Context

Found by the 14-repo housekeeping sweep of 2026-11-09 (19:05-19:15 UTC, run
from the ~/CNRS session). The ticket-only PRs that the harness 1481
native-prune rollout filed in adopter repos carry a `**Ticket:** NNNN` line
naming the very ticket the PR creates. The `/merge` close step runs
`erg close` on the ticket named by `**Ticket:**`, so landing such a PR by the
merge skill closes the new ticket at birth with its exit criteria unmet.

## Evidence

- fuzzy-corpus #74 and sen-causal-reading #171: merged, after review seats
  rewrote the line to `Ticket-ref:` by hand.
- chemin-de-voix #185 (ticket 0262): open, blocked on the close claim.
- padme #258 (ticket 0112): open, blocked on the close claim.
- AEDIST-technical-report #1198: open, blocked on the close claim, and it
  also reuses ticket number 0690 already on main, so it conflicts add/add on
  `tickets/.claims/0690`.

## Diagnosis

Established: the five PRs above carry `**Ticket:**` on the ticket they create
(two repaired by hand, three still open). Not established: which step of the
1481 filing flow writes the line (template, script or agent prompt), and how
the AEDIST PR picked a number already claimed on main (stale base or no
`erg next-id` against origin).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The ticket-filing flow writes `Ticket-ref:`, not `**Ticket:**`, on a PR that creates the ticket
- [ ] chemin-de-voix #185, padme #258 and AEDIST-technical-report #1198 are repaired (close claim rewritten; AEDIST renumbered off 0690)
- [ ] A test covers the filing flow's PR-body line
